	<section_number>18.2-504</section_number>
	<catch_line>Destroying or concealing wills</catch_line>
	<text>
		If any person fraudulently destroy or conceal any will or codicil, with intent to prevent the probate thereof, he shall be guilty of a Class 6 felony.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 18.1-309; 1960, c. 358; 1975, cc. 14, 15.</history>
</law>
